🔹 Step-by-Step Flow (per Coinbase Docs)
Client Requests Resource


Agent sends a standard HTTP request to a protected endpoint.
No credential yet = Pre-Mint state
Server Responds with HTTP 402 Payment Required


Response includes payment instructions (amount, currency, wallet address, TTL).
This is the Mint trigger — the server defines the credential conditions.
Client Submits Payment


Agent constructs a payment payload using its wallet (e.g., USDC on Base).
Payment is sent onchain and confirmed.
Client Resends Request with X-PAYMENT Header


Header includes proof of payment (e.g., transaction hash, signature).
This is the Validate step — server verifies payment and TTL.
Server Delivers Resource


If payment is valid and within TTL, access is granted.
Otherwise, access is denied or retried.
This mirrors your Mint-to Validate™ sequence:
Mint: Payment requirement issued
Validate: Proof of payment submitted
Access: Granted only if validation succeeds

